--TEST--
`Core\Router::signedRoute` verifies a signed link against the match the door already took and answers that match, so nothing reads the URL a second time — `rule:core-classes/router-signed-url`, `rule:routing/matched-once-before-the-handler`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The read half of `urlSigned`, over a request this same file makes. It takes
// no URL and no route name: what it verifies is the request this program is
// answering, so the only thing a caller can get wrong is the ring. The match it
// hands back is `Core\Request::route()`'s own — § 1 has the door take it once,
// before any application code runs, and a second match here would be a second
// answer about which route this is.
class Shop {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/shop/{id}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "Shop::show")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function show(int $id, #[Core\Query] string $page = ""): string { return $id as string; }
}

// Fixed rather than drawn, and the one thing about this shape that is not
// obvious: the program answering an in-process request is this same program run
// from the top (`rule:testing/in-process-request`), so a generated key would be
// a different key on the far side and nothing would ever verify.
secret bytes $key = Core\Bytes::fill(32, 65);
array<secret bytes> $ring = [$key];

// A capture and a leftover query parameter, because the payload covers both and
// a member that rebuilt only the captures would still verify a link with none.
string $link = Core\Router::urlSigned("Shop::show", ["id" => 7, "page" => "2"], {keys: $ring, until: null});

try {
    var $answered = Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, $link);
    echo "status ", $answered->status(), "\n";
    echo "body ", $answered->body(), "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
    // The child: the request the link names, answered by this file's own
    // script frame. What it echoes is the response body the parent prints.
    var $matched = Core\Router::signedRoute($ring);
    echo "route=", $matched->name() ?? "unnamed",
         " id=", $matched->param("id") ?? "none",
         " captures=", Core\Arr::count($matched->params()) as string;
}
--EXPECT--
status 200
body route=Shop::show id=7 captures=1
